<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1328–1708</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Gonzaga dynasty, Gonzaga family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Gonzaga was an Italian princely family that ruled Mantua from 1328 to 1708, first as captains, then as marquesses from 1433 and dukes from 1530. Its branches also held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a>, Guastalla, Novellara and, through Louis Gonzaga's marriage to Henriette of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> in 1565, the French duchy of Nevers. The family were major patrons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> artists such as Mantegna and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giulio-romano">Giulio Romano</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga.jpg" alt="House of Gonzaga" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Gianfrancesco_I_Gonzaga,_Marquess_of_Mantua.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
